WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.519
Every instance gets one of
three verdicts: retain it,

2
00:00:03.519 --> 00:00:06.988
consolidate its workload
into a target, or retire it.

3
00:00:06.988 --> 00:00:09.337
Three lenses make the call defensible.

4
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:10.550
How busy is it?

5
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.738
A database untouched for
over a year is a zombie,

6
00:00:13.738 --> 00:00:17.662
and retiring it removes every
forgotten login it carries.

7
00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:18.838
What version is it?

8
00:00:18.838 --> 00:00:21.920
Entra logins need SQL
Server 2022 or later,

9
00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.237
so most old engines are better
consolidated than upgraded.

10
00:00:26.237 --> 00:00:27.538
And what depends on it?

11
00:00:27.538 --> 00:00:31.613
A job that runs once a quarter can
make an idle instance load-bearing.

12
00:00:31.613 --> 00:00:36.675
The decision for the CIO and data
leadership: a verdict for every instance

13
00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:41.488
and a named target, so authentication
migrates once, in its final shape.

14
00:00:41.488 --> 00:00:42.550
Then the audit.
